Three bugs in liblocation:

- liblocation.so.0 named none of the libraries it uses (GLib, GObject,
  GConf, libdbus, dbus-glib): programs that did not link them themselves
  (a Qt program's plugin) failed to load it.
- dbus_g_proxy_call() takes the input arguments, G_TYPE_INVALID, then the
  output arguments and another G_TYPE_INVALID. The calls of location-ui's
  "display" and "close" ended after the inputs, so dbus-glib read whatever
  followed in the variable arguments as the first output's type. Where
  that is not 0 (on FreeBSD/arm64 it was not) every dialog request failed
  ("Too few arguments in reply") although location-ui showed the dialog;
  on Leste it worked only because that word happened to be 0.
- get_selected_method() had its test the wrong way round: a client's
  LOCATION_METHOD_USER_SELECTED (0, what most apps and liblocation's own
  example ask for) gave no method at all, a specific method every method.
  After the "enable positioning" dialog the user's yes therefore ended in
  LOCATION_ERROR_USER_REJECTED_DIALOG ("User didn't enable requested
  methods"), with GPS and network just switched on in GConf, and
  location_gpsd_control_get_allowed_methods() always returned 0. Now 0
  stands for every method the user allows (cell positioning only with the
  network allowed, so that the dialog answered with nothing still fails),
  a specific one for itself, as the code below the test already treats
  them.

The same fixes are in FreeBSD's Hildon build
(freebsd/hildon/patches/liblocation/0002, 0005, 0006).

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 0890b4b..25ba7e6 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ AC_PROG_CC
 AC_PROG_INSTALL
 AM_PROG_LIBTOOL
 
-PKG_CHECK_MODULES(LIBLOCATION, glib-2.0 gconf-2.0 dbus-glib-1)
+PKG_CHECK_MODULES(LIBLOCATION, glib-2.0 gobject-2.0 gconf-2.0 dbus-1 dbus-glib-1)
 AC_SUBST(LIBLOCATION_CFLAGS)
 AC_SUBST(LIBLOCATION_LIBS)
 
diff --git a/src/Makefile.am b/src/Makefile.am
index c2c6ee2..7b30e3c 100644
--- a/src/Makefile.am
+++ b/src/Makefile.am
@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@ liblocation_la_SOURCES = \
 	location-version.h
 
 liblocation_la_CFLAGS = $(LIBLOCATION_CFLAGS) -Wall
-liblocation_la_LDFLAGS = -lm -Wl,--as-needed
+liblocation_la_LDFLAGS = -Wl,--as-needed
+liblocation_la_LIBADD = $(LIBLOCATION_LIBS) -lm
 
 liblocationincludedir=$(includedir)/location
 liblocationinclude_HEADERS = \
